  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Unsettled weather is expected to return this \nweekend. \n\nA large ridge will remain overhead through much of the work \nweek maintaining warm and dry conditions. The ridge is expected \nto break down later in the week, allowing northern stream \nshortwave troughs to approach the Great Lakes region.\n\nBy the weekend, a deep southerly flow will likely move into the Ohio \nValley and the eastern Great Lakes region. While confidence is low \nregarding the timing of large scale forcing, daytime heating and \nincreasing moisture will likely support showers and thunderstorms \nduring the afternoon and evening hours. The chance for precipitation \nis higher inland from the Great Lakes. Ensemble Mean PWATS are \nforecast to be above 1.00\", which is around the 75th percentile for \nearly June. Any activity could produce heavy downpours. \n\nAn upper level trough may set-up across the region into early next \nweek and support continued chances for precipitation.",
